<title>BELGIUM: TESSENDERLO BUYS ENICHEM UNIT.</title>
<headline>TESSENDERLO BUYS ENICHEM UNIT.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian chemicals group Tessenderlo said on Monday it concluded an agreement with Italy's Enichem on the purchase of Enichem's chloride production unit in Pieve Vergonte in Italy for undisclosed terms.</p>
<p>The plant, with staff of 203 and annual sales of some 55 billion lira, makes chloro-toluenes and benzenes for phyto-sanitary products and the drugs industry.</p>
<p>It also has an electrolysis unit which allows it to have the chloride needed for bleaching locally available. The unit will strengthen Tessenderlo's position in bleached toluene derivatives.</p>
